# Privacy policy for this repo.
#
# EXCLUDED (never committed): protected health information, medical records,
# scanned evidence, and the filled case-facts file. These stay out of git
# history permanently.
#
# INCLUDED (deliberately): the patient's name and mailing address appear in
# ready-to-send letter templates. Those letters are meant to be printed and
# mailed, and the name and address are on the envelope anyway. Substituting
# placeholders would make them less usable.
#
# Consequence: this repo contains PII (name/address) but no PHI. It is safe to
# keep locally and to hand to an attorney. It should NOT be pushed to a public
# remote. If it ever needs to be published, scrub the name and address first --
# and note that rewriting git history would invalidate existing backup bundles,
# so make a fresh backup before doing so.

# Protected health information and case evidence must never enter git history.
disputes/**/evidence/*
!disputes/**/evidence/README.md

# Generated/filled correspondence containing real personal data.
# Templates are tracked; anything marked FILLED is not.
**/*.FILLED.md
**/*-FILLED.*

# Scans, records, exports
*.pdf
*.jpg
*.jpeg
*.png
*.tiff
*.zip

# macOS
.DS_Store
